# Same public DSL rule proved by FormalSQL (RuleSolver 51627d6).
# Strict Proj drops intermediate columns; it is NOT a safe native Compute
# replacement when its CBO target loses the source group's pass-through columns.
Proj<a0 s0 Item(Column(a2),a3,Item())>(Proj<a1 s1 Item(n0,a2,Item())>(Input<t0>))|Proj<a4 s2 Item(n0,a3,Item())>(Input<t1>)|t1 := t0;a4 := a0;s2 := s0
